1
00:00:00,067 --> 00:00:03,367
In 1977, an astronomer circled six characters

2
00:00:03,367 --> 00:00:04,533
on a telescope printout

3
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:06,933
and wrote one word beside them: Wow!

4
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:08,533
The signal never returned.

5
00:00:08,833 --> 00:00:10,467
And that's only one of seven cases

6
00:00:10,467 --> 00:00:11,633
where a small piece of evidence

7
00:00:11,633 --> 00:00:14,200
raises a question much bigger than the object itself.

8
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:17,567
At roughly 1,420 MHz,

9
00:00:17,867 --> 00:00:20,767
close to the frequency emitted by neutral hydrogen,

10
00:00:20,767 --> 00:00:26,267
Ohio State's Big Ear radio telescope detected
an unusually strong, narrowband signal.

11
00:00:26,267 --> 00:00:28,900
The date was August 15, 1977.

12
00:00:29,200 --> 00:00:32,700
Its intensity rose and fell
over a 72-second observation window,

13
00:00:32,700 --> 00:00:36,067
leaving the sequence 6EQUJ5 on a paper record.

14
00:00:36,233 --> 00:00:38,567
Jerry Ehman's handwritten reaction gave it a name.

15
00:00:38,833 --> 00:00:41,400
Repeated searches have failed to detect it again.

16
00:00:41,633 --> 00:00:43,000
That's the central difficulty:

17
00:00:43,167 --> 00:00:45,033
scientists have a genuine observation,

18
00:00:45,033 --> 00:00:46,933
but no second event to test against it.

19
00:00:46,933 --> 00:00:49,733
It might have been a natural astronomical phenomenon

20
00:00:49,733 --> 00:00:50,967
or interference.

21
00:00:50,967 --> 00:00:53,300
Some have suggested an artificial transmission,

22
00:00:53,300 --> 00:00:56,700
although there's no supporting
evidence of extraterrestrial technology.

23
00:00:56,867 --> 00:00:59,700
One burst left an extraordinary paper trail.

24
00:00:59,967 --> 00:01:02,333
A medieval manuscript offers the opposite puzzle:

25
00:01:02,333 --> 00:01:04,767
information everywhere, but no agreed meaning.

26
00:01:05,167 --> 00:01:09,067
About 240 pages survive in a manuscript held at Yale.

27
00:01:09,067 --> 00:01:11,133
They contain unfamiliar writing,

28
00:01:11,133 --> 00:01:14,800
diagrams of stars, and plants that are difficult to identify.

29
00:01:15,167 --> 00:01:17,433
The book is known as the Voynich Manuscript,

30
00:01:17,433 --> 00:01:20,267
after the dealer who acquired it in 1912.

31
00:01:20,433 --> 00:01:23,100
Tests date its parchment to the early 15th century.

32
00:01:23,300 --> 00:01:24,467
Here's the peculiar part:

33
00:01:24,467 --> 00:01:26,900
the frequency and arrangement of its word-like groups

34
00:01:27,167 --> 00:01:30,933
show statistical patterns resembling
those in natural languages.

35
00:01:30,933 --> 00:01:32,400
Yet no proposed translation

36
00:01:32,400 --> 00:01:34,600
has won broad scholarly acceptance.

37
00:01:34,833 --> 00:01:36,900
A real language, an elaborate cipher,

38
00:01:36,900 --> 00:01:38,600
or carefully constructed nonsense

39
00:01:38,600 --> 00:01:40,567
could account for different parts of the evidence;

40
00:01:40,567 --> 00:01:43,133
the statistical patterns alone don't settle the matter.

41
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:44,500
The writing has structure.

42
00:01:44,500 --> 00:01:46,067
Its meaning remains inaccessible.

43
00:01:46,433 --> 00:01:47,800
Now imagine an ancient object

44
00:01:47,800 --> 00:01:49,367
whose function can be reconstructed,

45
00:01:49,367 --> 00:01:52,033
even though the people who designed
it have disappeared from the record.

46
00:01:52,433 --> 00:01:54,833
Roughly 30 surviving bronze gears

47
00:01:54,833 --> 00:01:56,833
lie inside the fragments of a device

48
00:01:56,833 --> 00:02:00,033
recovered from a Greek shipwreck in 1901.

49
00:02:00,033 --> 00:02:01,500
The Antikythera Mechanism

50
00:02:01,500 --> 00:02:03,633
was built about 2,000 years ago.

51
00:02:03,633 --> 00:02:04,833
Some of its gear teeth

52
00:02:04,833 --> 00:02:07,033
are only about 1.5 mm long.

53
00:02:07,367 --> 00:02:08,233
Turn a handle,

54
00:02:08,233 --> 00:02:10,867
and linked gears could display astronomical cycles,

55
00:02:10,867 --> 00:02:12,700
including the movements of the Sun and Moon

56
00:02:12,700 --> 00:02:14,233
and predictions of eclipses.

57
00:02:14,233 --> 00:02:16,767
These functions are supported by surviving inscriptions

58
00:02:16,767 --> 00:02:17,867
and physical fragments.

59
00:02:18,033 --> 00:02:19,767
The astonishing gap is historical:

60
00:02:19,933 --> 00:02:21,433
nothing comparably complex

61
00:02:21,433 --> 00:02:22,967
is known in the surviving record

62
00:02:22,967 --> 00:02:25,267
for more than 1,000 years afterward.

63
00:02:25,267 --> 00:02:27,500
Researchers can model its missing mechanisms,

64
00:02:27,500 --> 00:02:30,633
but those reconstructions aren't identical to an intact original.

65
00:02:30,900 --> 00:02:32,433
We still can't identify its maker

66
00:02:32,433 --> 00:02:34,833
or know how common such devices once were.

67
00:02:35,067 --> 00:02:37,567
This bronze machine was built to describe the sky.

68
00:02:37,567 --> 00:02:38,600
The next trail of clues

69
00:02:38,600 --> 00:02:40,500
would be found in the snow of the Ural Mountains.

70
00:02:40,867 --> 00:02:41,933
Nine hikers died

71
00:02:41,933 --> 00:02:43,233
in the northern Ural Mountains

72
00:02:43,233 --> 00:02:44,900
in February 1959.

73
00:02:45,100 --> 00:02:47,267
When rescuers found their campsite weeks later,

74
00:02:47,267 --> 00:02:49,067
the tent had been cut from the inside.

75
00:02:49,067 --> 00:02:51,067
Boots and winter clothing were left behind,

76
00:02:51,067 --> 00:02:53,400
and footprints led downhill through the snow.

77
00:02:53,667 --> 00:02:56,133
Several victims had suffered serious injuries.

78
00:02:56,300 --> 00:02:58,833
Russian prosecutors concluded in 2020

79
00:02:58,833 --> 00:03:01,567
that an avalanche had driven the group from the tent.

80
00:03:01,567 --> 00:03:04,633
A scientific model published in 2021

81
00:03:04,633 --> 00:03:06,200
showed how wind-loaded snow

82
00:03:06,200 --> 00:03:08,800
could release a small slab above their shelter.

83
00:03:08,800 --> 00:03:10,733
But the slope appeared relatively gentle,

84
00:03:10,733 --> 00:03:13,467
and searchers reported no obvious avalanche debris.

85
00:03:13,633 --> 00:03:16,300
The researchers offered mechanisms for those objections;

86
00:03:16,433 --> 00:03:19,533
their model still can't reproduce
every decision made that night.

87
00:03:19,533 --> 00:03:22,133
A sudden snow hazard is a credible explanation.

88
00:03:22,133 --> 00:03:24,267
The precise sequence remains uncertain.

89
00:03:24,467 --> 00:03:26,800
From a mountain with too little visible debris,

90
00:03:26,800 --> 00:03:29,400
the trail leads to a forest covered in evidence

91
00:03:29,400 --> 00:03:30,733
of an enormous blast.

92
00:03:31,067 --> 00:03:32,933
On June 30, 1908,

93
00:03:32,933 --> 00:03:34,467
an explosion over Siberia

94
00:03:34,467 --> 00:03:37,567
flattened roughly 2,000 km² of forest

95
00:03:37,567 --> 00:03:38,800
near the Tunguska River.

96
00:03:38,800 --> 00:03:40,833
When investigators finally reached the area,

97
00:03:40,833 --> 00:03:43,067
they found trees lying outward from the blast zone

98
00:03:43,067 --> 00:03:44,200
in a broad radial pattern.

99
00:03:44,200 --> 00:03:46,500
But there was no obvious impact crater.

100
00:03:46,733 --> 00:03:49,567
That missing crater once made the event seem impossible.

101
00:03:49,567 --> 00:03:51,400
The leading scientific explanation

102
00:03:51,400 --> 00:03:54,333
is an asteroid breaking apart above the ground,

103
00:03:54,333 --> 00:03:56,800
releasing its energy into the atmosphere.

104
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:59,733
The fallen trees support a powerful airburst;

105
00:03:59,733 --> 00:04:03,167
the exact size, composition,
and trajectory of the incoming body

106
00:04:03,167 --> 00:04:05,733
have to be estimated from the remaining evidence.

107
00:04:05,733 --> 00:04:07,833
A massive disturbance can leave a clear pattern

108
00:04:07,833 --> 00:04:09,933
without leaving an intact object behind.

109
00:04:10,300 --> 00:04:12,867
The next disappearance also left almost no trace

110
00:04:12,867 --> 00:04:13,867
of the person involved,

111
00:04:14,400 --> 00:04:16,300
except for money recovered beside a river.

112
00:04:16,733 --> 00:04:18,200
$5,800

113
00:04:18,200 --> 00:04:19,667
in damaged $20 bills

114
00:04:19,667 --> 00:04:22,300
turned up beside the Columbia River in 1980.

115
00:04:22,300 --> 00:04:23,367
Their serial numbers

116
00:04:23,367 --> 00:04:25,067
matched money given to a hijacker

117
00:04:25,067 --> 00:04:26,133
nine years earlier.

118
00:04:26,367 --> 00:04:28,833
On November 24, 1971,

119
00:04:28,833 --> 00:04:30,367
a man traveling as Dan Cooper

120
00:04:30,367 --> 00:04:32,933
took control of a Boeing 727 flight,

121
00:04:32,933 --> 00:04:34,867
demanded $200,000

122
00:04:34,867 --> 00:04:36,033
and 4 parachutes,

123
00:04:36,033 --> 00:04:37,733
then released the passengers in Seattle.

124
00:04:37,733 --> 00:04:39,167
The plane departed again.

125
00:04:39,433 --> 00:04:41,300
Somewhere over the Pacific Northwest,

126
00:04:41,300 --> 00:04:42,500
he jumped into the night.

127
00:04:42,733 --> 00:04:44,767
The recovered bills are confirmed evidence,

128
00:04:44,767 --> 00:04:46,800
but they don't tell us whether Cooper survived

129
00:04:46,800 --> 00:04:47,867
or identify him.

130
00:04:48,100 --> 00:04:51,033
The FBI considered a fatal landing plausible.

131
00:04:51,267 --> 00:04:55,533
In 2016, the bureau redirected
resources to other investigations

132
00:04:55,533 --> 00:04:57,133
while preserving the case information.

133
00:04:57,133 --> 00:04:58,800
The bills reached a riverbank.

134
00:04:58,933 --> 00:05:00,867
Where Cooper went is another question.

135
00:05:00,867 --> 00:05:03,867
And the last case replaces a river with a vast stretch of ocean.

136
00:05:04,300 --> 00:05:05,867
239 people

137
00:05:05,867 --> 00:05:08,767
were aboard Malaysia Airlines Flight 370

138
00:05:08,767 --> 00:05:11,033
when it disappeared on March 8, 2014,

139
00:05:11,033 --> 00:05:13,400
flying from Kuala Lumpur to Beijing.

140
00:05:13,400 --> 00:05:14,833
Satellite data indicated

141
00:05:14,833 --> 00:05:16,900
a route toward the southern Indian Ocean.

142
00:05:17,133 --> 00:05:18,667
In July 2015,

143
00:05:18,967 --> 00:05:21,667
a wing component washed ashore on Réunion Island.

144
00:05:21,867 --> 00:05:23,533
Investigators confirmed it came

145
00:05:23,533 --> 00:05:25,600
from the missing Boeing 777.

146
00:05:25,600 --> 00:05:30,067
Yet the main wreckage, flight recorders,
and exact crash location remain unlocated.

147
00:05:30,067 --> 00:05:32,667
The debris is physical evidence of the aircraft's fate;

148
00:05:32,667 --> 00:05:35,567
explanations for why it changed course remain unproven.

149
00:05:35,567 --> 00:05:37,500
The multinational underwater search

150
00:05:37,500 --> 00:05:39,300
was suspended in 2017.

151
00:05:39,467 --> 00:05:42,733
The latest search ended in January 2026

152
00:05:42,733 --> 00:05:44,133
without finding the aircraft.

153
00:05:44,133 --> 00:05:47,600
Five months later, Malaysia extended
its agreement with Ocean Infinity

154
00:05:47,600 --> 00:05:49,167
through June 2027,

155
00:05:49,433 --> 00:05:52,600
leaving thousands of square kilometers still to examine.

156
00:05:52,833 --> 00:05:54,933
More than 12 years after the disappearance,

157
00:05:54,933 --> 00:05:56,500
the main wreckage remains missing.

158
00:05:56,767 --> 00:05:59,633
For the families of the 239 people aboard,

159
00:05:59,633 --> 00:06:01,233
every new search carries the hope

160
00:06:01,233 --> 00:06:02,800
of finally learning what happened.

161
00:06:03,200 --> 00:06:06,300
A radio signal lasted 72 seconds.

162
00:06:06,300 --> 00:06:08,733
A manuscript survived 6 centuries.

163
00:06:08,733 --> 00:06:10,700
An ancient machine preserved its gears,

164
00:06:10,700 --> 00:06:11,700
and a missing aircraft

165
00:06:11,700 --> 00:06:13,333
left pieces on distant shores.

166
00:06:13,600 --> 00:06:15,300
Each clue brings us closer to an event

167
00:06:15,300 --> 00:06:16,667
we can no longer witness.

168
00:06:16,667 --> 00:06:18,700
The next discovery may change a theory,

169
00:06:19,067 --> 00:06:19,967
settle a question,

170
00:06:20,333 --> 00:06:22,267
or reveal that we've been asking the wrong one.
